  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BBB Nicaragua</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="6" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collaboration between the partners of the DTZ Alliance trough ICCO and Fly Free Movement has been consolidated since 2014 during the regional meetings, learning exchanges and interaction through the digital platform, in these spaces the experiences and strengths that each partner has have been shared, however, the most direct space for collaboration is between the Alliance and the implementing partners at the country level because country teams know the specific strengths of each of the partners. The partners strengthen their learning areas in order to enhance their capacities and abilities in the area of CSEC and the impact that COVID-19 has generated on children and adolescents in order to contribute to respond to the effects on children and adolescents caused by the pandemic, the partners consolidate their actions based on an institutional care protocol for COVID-19.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">San Rafael del Sur is a municipality in the department of Managua in Nicaragua, the beaches of Masachapa and Pochomil are popular tourist places for national and foreign population, the main economic activities are artisanal fishing and tourism, however, the COVID-19 pandemic negatively impacted causing: reduction of national and foreign tourism; reduction of the workforce at Barcel&#xF3; Montelimar hotel and the Montelimar sugar mill, causing unemployment in the families of the communities</narrative>
  </description>
